From: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
Date: Sat, 14 Nov 2026 08:48:40 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] ext-nosrc landing edit LE-width: re-wrap one statement line
 of Extraction/Sampler

The delivery adds one line over 100 characters (Sampler.lean:105, 102 characters, in the
statement of chooseWord's flatten lemma). Re-wrapped; whitespace only, no change to any
statement, proof or name.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01PqpVTiuDcjSqhyfbqnsVxA
---
 TCSlib/Cryptography/Randomness/Extraction/Sampler.lean | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/TCSlib/Cryptography/Randomness/Extraction/Sampler.lean b/TCSlib/Cryptography/Randomness/Extraction/Sampler.lean
index 92bbe93f4..2f4e27286 100644
--- a/TCSlib/Cryptography/Randomness/Extraction/Sampler.lean
+++ b/TCSlib/Cryptography/Randomness/Extraction/Sampler.lean
@@ -102,7 +102,8 @@ the same branch choice; induction identifies the remaining trials. -/
 theorem chooseWord_flatten (Ext : List Bool → List Bool) (n t : ℕ)
     (x : Fin (t + 1) → Fin n → Bool) :
     chooseWord Ext n t (List.ofFn fun i => List.ofFn (x i)).flatten =
-      List.ofFn (Rejection.select (fun a : Fin n → Bool => (Ext (List.ofFn a)).headD false) t x) := by
+      List.ofFn
+        (Rejection.select (fun a : Fin n → Bool => (Ext (List.ofFn a)).headD false) t x) := by
   induction t with
   | zero =>
     rw [Rejection.select_zero, List.ofFn_succ, List.ofFn_zero, List.flatten_cons,
